title: Ramu_Day1
tags: 
position: 626,-302
---
<<PlayBackgroundMusic Light_3>>
<<SetBGSprite HutInterior>>
<<HideCharacter>>

Dawn breaks over their small home. Raju awakens to sounds of the bustling slum. Through thin walls, he hears Ramu already moving about in their makeshift cricket practice ground.

<<HideCharacter>>

First rays of sunlight filter through narrow gaps between buildings. Raju finds Ramu arranging makeshift cricket equipment in the tiny courtyard space.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Arre, stop lazing around!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: If you want to play cricket, you need practice. Every single day.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Talent means nothing without hard work.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: But... I'm tired, bhaiya.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: Yesterday's practice went so late. Can't I rest today?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: Just this once?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Rest? Do you think Sunil Gavaskar rested when he was your age?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Do you think Kapil Dev took days off when he was learning to bowl?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Hah! No, they practiced until their hands bled.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: And their legs gave out.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Every minute you waste lying around is a minute some other boy is getting better.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Some boy who wants it more than you.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: Some boy who doesn't make excuses.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: The boys from the rich schools, they have coaches, proper equipment, everything.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Angry>>
Ramu: What do we have? Only determination.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Only the willingness to work harder than everyone else.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: I understand, bhaiya.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: I do want this. I want to be good enough to make you proud.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Proud? Pride is a luxury we can't afford.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Not until you've earned it.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: But... yes, I want you to succeed. More than you know.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Good. Now remember - elbow up, feet balanced.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Watch the ball, always watch the ball.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: And remember this feeling, this morning, when practice is hard and you want to quit.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Champions are made in moments like this.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: What if I'm not good enough, bhaiya?

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Sad>>
Raju: What if all this practice doesn't matter?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Then at least we'll know we tried.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: At least we'll know that we didn't let fear stop us.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: But I've watched you play, little brother. You have something special.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Something that can't be bought or taught.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: You just need to believe in it as much as I do.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: There! Did you feel that?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: That's what I'm talking about!

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: That timing, that natural swing - you can't teach that.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: But you can perfect it.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: I felt it, bhaiya. It felt... right.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Then remember that feeling. Hold onto it.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Because that feeling is going to carry you further than any fancy equipment.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Further than expensive coaching ever could.

<<HideCharacter>>

As the first morning's practice concludes, both understand they've begun something significant - a serious training regimen that could determine if talent becomes skill.

