For the eighth consecutive morning, Raju meets his brother for practice. Today carries special weight - Ramu will either commit to tournament registration or suggest waiting.

The familiar pre-dawn atmosphere carries unprecedented significance. Both understand this will be a decisive practice session.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: Seven days ago, when you first asked me to help with cricket...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: I thought it was just another kid's fantasy.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: But I've watched you choose to wake up early every single morning.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Choose to practice when other kids are still sleeping.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Choose to listen and improve instead of just playing around.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: I meant everything I said, bhai.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Serious>>
Raju: Cricket isn't just play for me - it's my dream.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Smiling>>
Raju: And you've helped me understand what it takes to chase dreams properly.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: The tournament registration closes tomorrow.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: The entry fee is fifty rupees.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Sad>>
Ramu: Money our family doesn't have to waste on uncertain dreams.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: But after seven days of watching you prove your commitment...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: After seeing our neighbors stop their morning routines to watch you practice...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: After witnessing how seriously you take every piece of advice...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: I'm convinced this isn't uncertain anymore.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: You really think I'm ready?

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: I think you've been ready for a week.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Serious>>
Ramu: The question was whether I was ready to believe in you.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Seven mornings of watching you choose cricket over sleep...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: Improvement over comfort, discipline over fun...

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: You've answered every doubt I had.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: I'll find the fifty rupees. I'll register you tomorrow morning.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Smiling>>
Ramu: And I'll be there cheering when you play.

<<SetCharacterExpression Ramu Excited>>
Ramu: Knowing that every shot you make comes from the dedication you've shown me this week.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Excited>>
Raju: Thank you, bhai. For believing in me.

<<SetCharacterExpression Raju Smiling>>
